<section class="feature-copy-grid" aria-labelledby="security-verify-title">
  <div>
    <h2
      id="security-verify-title"
    >
      Check that a download is really ours.
    </h2>
  </div>
  <ul class="feature-copy-list">
    <article>
      <h3>Every release ships its evidence.</h3><p>
        Blanc releases on <a
          href="https://github.com/bnfy/blanc/releases"
          rel="noopener">GitHub</a
        > include a <code>SHA256SUMS</code> manifest covering every artifact, a Sigstore
        bundle authenticating that manifest, a software bill of materials, and platform
        signatures — an Apple Developer ID on macOS, an Authenticode signature on
        Windows. <a
          href="https://github.com/bnfy/blanc/blob/main/docs/release-verification.md"
          rel="noopener">Step-by-step verification instructions</a
        > live in the repository.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>The signing identity, on the record.</h3><p>
        Release manifests are signed keylessly via Sigstore. A genuine Blanc
        release verifies against exactly this identity and issuer — published
        here, independently of any release, so a tampered download cannot vouch
        for itself:
      </p><p>
        <!--email_off-->
        <code>anthony@bnfy.me</code><!--/email_off--> via <code
          >https://github.com/login/oauth</code>
      </p>
    </article>
  </ul>
</section>

<aside class="truth-note" aria-labelledby="security-note-title">
  <h2 id="security-note-title">
    Private by architecture, not by magic.
  </h2><p>
    No browser can make you anonymous on its own. Blanc reduces what runs inside
    the browser and what leaves your device; it does not hide your traffic from
    your network, your employer, or your internet provider. If you use a VPN you
    trust, Blanc runs quietly underneath it.
  </p><a
    class="text-link"
    href="/privacy"
    data-track="feature_cta_click"
    data-feature="security"
    data-cta-position="truth-note"
    >Read the full privacy policy <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
</aside>
